+          "label": "Revised",
+          "text": "2026-10-26 (T-3175, piece 1 of T-3172) — **the pavilion's roof is built.** The pavilion is carried up an attic storey past the main cornice, three tall lights in its wall, under a steep slated roof hipped on every side to a point with a turned iron finial (`form.mansard`'s `crown`), its heights and its lights read off the photograph through the same camera. Invented: how far the crown runs back into the main roof (6.0 m, so its ridge is about 0.5 m long; the photograph sees it end on), its 47-degree pitch (the photograph reads about 45, the kit's steep range starts over 45), its cornice standing 0.65 m past the pavilion's sides (the kit's least; the photograph's stands about at them), the attic's wall in stone across the pavilion's whole width (the photograph slates its outer parts as cheeks), the lights' flat transoms (the photograph's are arched) and the finial's turning (the deck's, T-3000). The corner block and its tower remain unbuilt: T-3176."
         }
       ],
