+      "note": "Through the photograph's camera: the slated lower faces rise steeply from the cornice (about 12.6 m) to the curb (about 16.8 m); a dormer under a pediment stands on the front over the window bay south of the pavilion (x 650-770 px) and another over the porch at the north end (x 190-250 px). T-3175: the pavilion's crown, read off the photograph through its camera: the pavilion is carried up an attic from the main eave (12.6 m, y 845 px) to its own cornice at about y 605 px (16.8 m, the main curb's height; attic_m 4.2), under a steep slated roof hipped on every side from that cornice (x 350-597 px) to a point at about y 410 px (about 20.2 m) with a turned iron finial to about y 355 px (about 1 m). Built as K05's hipped crown: 47 degrees on the sides and the street end (the photograph's rise of about 3.4 m over a half-width of about 3.4 m reads 45 degrees; 47 is the nearest the kit's steep range allows, its ridge about 20.5 m), the cornice 0.65 m past the pavilion's face and sides (the kit's least past the main cornice's 0.6 m; the photograph's stands about at the pavilion's sides), run 6.0 m back into the main roof so its ridge is about 0.5 m long (the photograph sees it end on, as a point). How far it runs back, which no picture shows, is reconstructed."
